{"title":"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232b5550b915f4e687674171d9c44f5e0e72bc6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^5 + by^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> if the real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a7fa4d4202b4ee46cc9c480239c5e9fcea5db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy the equations\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324d4fe0e034cdfc99f59ab1a6bf99cef7ed8cfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} ax + by &amp;= 3, \\\\ ax^2 + by^2 &amp;= 7, \\\\ ax^3 + by^3 &amp;= 16, \\\\ ax^4 + by^4 &amp;= 42. \\end{align*}\" width=\"120\" height=\"99\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/84915e4ad8bdd41a0226f342f072679253131f47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = (x + y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d3097842fc0c9322725afddee258fb3732f76b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />. Then the relationship\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f94325db6aeef76228724001b80602f820fddc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ax^n + by^n)(x + y) = (ax^{n + 1} + by^{n + 1}) + (xy)(ax^{n - 1} + by^{n - 1})\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>can be exploited:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cffa563b7d4bc1f4507c64f2239d30510c20ea5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}(ax^2 + by^2)(x + y) &amp; = &amp; (ax^3 + by^3) + (xy)(ax + by) \\\\ (ax^3 + by^3)(x + y) &amp; = &amp; (ax^4 + by^4) + (xy)(ax^2 + by^2)\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"423\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Therefore:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c50e24eff3e9489b94f3fb1d53f74024c52bbc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}7S &amp; = &amp; 16 + 3P \\\\ 16S &amp; = &amp; 42 + 7P\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"140\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a230b379e2a801454e69eaf4ad8ea7db0a76dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378056232528e0abdfeca1463fe8cd9592a70aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = - 38$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />. Finally:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957cd00cb367a3ed09b82409f81bfd0e73723084.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}(ax^4 + by^4)(x + y) &amp; = &amp; (ax^5 + by^5) + (xy)(ax^3 + by^3) \\\\ (42)(S) &amp; = &amp; (ax^5 + by^5) + (P)(16) \\\\ (42)( - 14) &amp; = &amp; (ax^5 + by^5) + ( - 38)(16) \\\\ ax^5 + by^5 &amp; = &amp; \\boxed{020}\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"423\" height=\"99\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Linear_recurrence\" title=\"Linear recurrence\"> recurrence</a> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904cc6a6739fd4ea74b08b661e0a05493814027d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n=AT_{n-1}+BT_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" /> will have the closed form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f44d55a8ae42b16d34721930da955aae66b37fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n=ax^n+by^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> are the values of the starting term that make the sequence geometric, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are the appropriately chosen constants such that those special starting terms linearly combine to form the actual starting terms and match the original equations.\n</p><p>Suppose we have such a recurrence with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c1185c2b9c628117ca74d835b278407185649984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e15e172d00c7b9a4747302e919ac70d013b3585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472ac9d26fe05fbbbfde3732ea52ada0a2ce7f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_3=ax^3+by^3=16=7A+3B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517317012ed21cbd9bfa9fd5451a58717e8ac079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_4=ax^4+by^4=42=16A+7B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Solving these simultaneous equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/3307c205be298f1c4a63ae0e60c19bfee1cdbb3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=-14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb63921c36081202a45ee47c8dceffac6c5bd5c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=38$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbb542f57e9473004bd8a1d82f6ae63e82af536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^5+by^5=T_5=-14(42)+38(16)= \\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"343\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Edits-Amon26\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using factoring formulas, the terms can be grouped. First take the first three terms and sum them, getting:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db16c80e6a44fe5eebbefded73ae65314ca884bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(x^3 + x^2 + x) + b(y^3 + y^2 + y) = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/3752a7ede12249ed39ae11a8f8135689256018db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax\\left( \\frac{x^3-1}{x-1} \\right) + by\\left( \\frac{y^3-1}{y-1} \\right) = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"268\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly take the first two terms, yielding:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93fe245e4b1a08e7c3d7493926cb9b9ae23d9e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax \\left( \\frac{x^2-1}{x-1} \\right) + by \\left( \\frac{y^2-1}{y-1} \\right) = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"268\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Lastly take an alternating three-term sum,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d0b4fd29568f5a3a70a897760f6fe6c82825b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(x^3 - x^2 + x) + b(y^3 - y^2 + y) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128a08306320eb06d41758a6332c75d63159be88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax \\left( \\frac{x^3+1}{x+1} \\right) + by \\left( \\frac{y^3+1}{y+1} \\right) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"268\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Now to get the solution, let the answer be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e73801d98562089857b7d5029376ef4856bbd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax \\left( \\frac{x^4-1}{x-1} \\right) + by \\left(\\frac{y^4-1}{y-1} \\right) = 68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"268\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying out this expression gets the answer term and then a lot of other expressions, which can be eliminated\nas done in the first solution.\n</p><p>~lpieleanu (reformatting and minor edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first let the answer to this problem be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> Multiplying the first equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/65045fc1919e6c59dfb0aee3140da40168626578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2 + bxy=3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Subtracting this equation from the second equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce57b846ee825cb68276acd3e6ded09f1643cb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^2-bxy=7-3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />. Similarly, doing the same for the other equations, we obtain:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce57b846ee825cb68276acd3e6ded09f1643cb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^2-bxy=7-3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e16505942f0493599c8764eef392708a723396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^3-bxy^2=16-7x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b683d2971e77888a731a34d6644de0bd427ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^4-bxy^3=42-16x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb5561b5f945b9a9ed165632c29a6417aab5420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^5-bxy^4=k-42x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow lets take the first equation. Multiplying this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and subtracting this from the second gives us  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d1951bfa79f1f3c981582e7eefcda08e0af85b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^3-bxy^2=(7-3x)y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />. We can also obtain  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3a64f07554adf8d15648a454cbe64654438cba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by^4-bxy^3=(16-7x)y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Now we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />! <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d02ed5e2b8be9be24cc2088325a8d4de9ff5e749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7-3x)y = 16-7x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb717a16b2e07ca239e0a4e0bedf9b84eb9ef321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(16-7x)y=42-16x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/58635fc8deaf89fe6cea966600be61219d8dbf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-7+\\sqrt{87},-7-\\sqrt{87})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" /> (It can be switched, but since the given equations are symmetric, it doesn't matter). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e1834e65e3bb89d31cfbc689026bc72f527e19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-42x= (42-16x)y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />, and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e3197bd89719e94f1dd2c0f328aaa84eea69d73f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k= \\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~pi_is_3.141\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME\" title=\"1990 AIME\">1990 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1990 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1990\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/P